\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 1) Fix digital and information gaps:}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto
\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb60\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 More than half of PWDs rated accessibility below 50%, and 8 in 10 were unaware of existing training or hiring grants. To address this gap, the study recommends developing a national "Inclusion Gateway", a unified digital portal that connects job opportunities, grants, and training programmes. The platform would feature SMS or Whatsapp prompts that guide users step-by-step and be co-tested by PWD users.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb60\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj
